<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126"><tei:pb n="472" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n496_medium.jpg"/><tei:head xml:lang="en">Psalm 126</tei:head><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/1"/>A Pilgrim Song. When the Lord brought the exiles back to Zion, we were like those who dream. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/2"/>Our mouth was filled with laughter, and our tongue with ringing song; then it was said among the nations: “The Lord has done great things for them.” <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/3"/>The Lord had done great things for us, and we rejoiced. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/4"/>Restore our fortunes O Lord, like streams in the Negev. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/5"/>Those who are sowing in tears shall reap in joy. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/126/6"/>Sadly the farmer bears the bag of seed to the field; he shall come home with joy, bearing his sheaves. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
